# LIVELITS #
# A livelit is a live GUI widget which can be inserted into expressions. #
# It elaborates to a value of some given type. #

# Invocation: #
# To invoke a livelit, insert the name of the livelit (always prefixed with ^) then space. #
# The context inspector shows which livelits are available and their elaboration type. #

# Each livelit maintains an internal model, which is not generally something the #
# programmer should need to look at. You can see the internal model by toggling #
# the livelit projector off (bottom right corner of Hazel). #

# Livelits are DEFINED IN THE PROGRAM: a module bound to a livelit name #
# provides init, update, view, and expand members, plus an optional #
# shape -- Inline(w), Block(w, h), or Tab(w, h) -- for its footprint. #
# The following slides each define one. #

# Five livelits ship built in, each reaching something Hazel itself cannot #
# say: one evaluates JavaScript, and four run Fumola. #

# ^js #
# Elaboration Type: String                                    #
# Elaboration: The result of evaluating the code as JavaScript. #
# Internal Model: (String, String) -- the code and its result.  #
let greeting = ^^livelit(^js("['hi', 'from js'].join(' ')", "hi from js")) in

# The Fumola livelits #
# Fumola is an experimental language whose execution model is Adapton:    #
# a run leaves behind a graph of what it named, read and demanded, and    #
# the next run repairs that graph instead of redoing the work. Four       #
# livelits run Fumola programs inside a Hazel one:                        #
#                                                                         #
#   ^fumola_new(id, mode)             declare a runtime                   #
#   ^fumola_put_force(id, name, src)  run src in a named thunk            #
#   ^fumola_eval(id, src)             run src on a force-free stack       #
#   ^fumola_with(id, name, src, v)    the same, with v bound as input     #
#                                                                         #
# Each names the runtime it talks to by id, so livelits sharing an id     #
# share one runtime, and the state written through one is there for the   #
# next. ^fumola_new expands to that id, and its mode -- Simple or         #
# Graphical -- says which Adapton semantics that runtime runs; the other  #
# three expand to whatever their type annotation says, so each needs one. #
#                                                                         #
# These are built in because they drive a Fumola runtime compiled to      #
# wasm, outside Hazel; see scripts/build-fumola-wasm.sh. The Fumola       #
# (Livelits) slides take them one idea at a time, with examples.          #
greeting
